title: Most of setup's "start the Skg server" is for someone who has run it before, and its paths are written from two different folders.
pid: 502f8a07-a466-48f5-b36b-8ed228d614db
body: |2-
  Misspelled config keys and an old spelling of one, an environment
  variable "that used to select release" and is gone, the compiled
  elisp's Emacs version and the native-compilation cache: history and
  pitfalls before the reader has seen it work (c). The command is
  written '../bash/start-servers.sh', from inside 'docs/', and the
  next sentence says to run it from the top of the repository, where
  '../bash' is outside it; the stop script is then given from the top.
  The client's snippet, '../elisp/skg-reload.el', works only if
  evaluated from inside 'setup.org' (as Org's C-c C-c would), which
  the page does not say.
  Change: keep the command, written from the top of the repository,
  and what the reader sees when it works (the first build takes
  minutes and sits at "Validating config"); move the rest to
  'docs/troubleshooting/'. Say where to evaluate the snippet.
